Greetings all,

Is there a way to generate shape coordinates for a point on a plot of a PLS generated using phylo.integration?

I'm coming back to warping a reference mesh to the shapes at the positive and negative extremes of a PLS axis and running into issues generating coordinates for  plotRefToTarget, as discussed in this old conversation. <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/hAYaForjkmY/m/LmyQ0r_-CgAJ>

As far as I know, shape.predictor is not able to function the way I need it to, since I cannot correct the PLS that it runs for phylogeny as you can while using the phylo.integration function. Neither shapes=TRUE in the argument nor picknplot.shape will work for surfaces so those are also a no-go.

The output values of phylo.integraton and two.b.pls are essentially the same as in the older verison of geomorph, but my old work around from the linked conversation is no longer working. I haven't figured out why yet, but I figured I would post up here to see if there was a simpler solution to do what I need while I trouble shoot my old work around.

Thanks for any help,
-Jasmine

From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Wed Apr 20 11:18:53 2022
From: uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com (Mike Collyer)
Date: Wed, 20 Apr 2022 11:18:53 +0000
Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] Warping meshes using PLS from phylo.integration
Message-ID: <U-pgptrZE9I.IQFNMWkvGwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <U-pgptrZE9I.ouZYYjcDGwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <U-pgptrZE9I.ouZYYjcDGwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/U-pgptrZE9I/m/IQFNMWkvGwAJ>
